Subject: [PATCH] egl/surfaceless: kms_swrast on tegra

The decoder process of Firefox checks that it can import the pictures of the
video decoder with EGL, in a sandbox where the GPU of a Tegra is out of reach.
EGL then falls back to software rendering, but without DRM, so without dma-buf
imports, and Firefox gives up hardware decoding. With kms_swrast, as on
virtio_gpu, the import works.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
18:02:49
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
@@ -272,14 +272,19 @@ surfaceless_probe_device(_EGLDisplay *di
 
       disp->Device = dev_list;
       if (swrast) {
-         /* Use kms swrast only with vgem / virtio_gpu.
+         /* Use kms swrast only with vgem / virtio_gpu / tegra.
           * virtio-gpu fallbacks to software rendering when 3D features
           * are unavailable since 6c5ab, and kms_swrast is more
           * feature complete than swrast.
+          * tegra: where a sandbox hides the GPU (the decoder process of
+          * Firefox), the pictures of the video decoder can still be imported.
           */
-         if (driver_name && (strcmp(driver_name, "vgem") == 0 ||
-                             strcmp(driver_name, "virtio_gpu") == 0))
+         char *kernel_name = loader_get_kernel_driver_name(dri2_dpy->fd_render_gpu);
+         if ((driver_name && (strcmp(driver_name, "vgem") == 0 ||
+                              strcmp(driver_name, "virtio_gpu") == 0)) ||
+             (kernel_name && strcmp(kernel_name, "tegra") == 0))
             dri2_dpy->driver_name = strdup("kms_swrast");
+         free(kernel_name);
          free(driver_name);
       } else {
          /* Use the given hardware driver */
